{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-108336","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174404","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-108337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174405","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-174406","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-174407","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-174408","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-174409","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-174410","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-108338","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174411","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-108339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174412","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-174413","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-174414","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-108340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174415","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-174416","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-108341","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174417","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-174418","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-174419","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-108342","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-108343","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174420","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-108344","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-108345","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174421","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-108346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174422","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-108347","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174423","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-108348","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174424","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-174425","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-174426","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-108349","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174427","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-108351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174428","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-108353","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174429","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-108355","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174430","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-108357","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108359","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174431","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-108360","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174432","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-174433","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-174434","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-108361","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174435","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-174436","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-108363","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174437","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-108365","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174438","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-108367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174439","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-108369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174440","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-108371","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108373","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174441","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-108374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174442","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-174443","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-174444","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-108375","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-108376","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174445","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-108377","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174446","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-108378","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174447","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-174448","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-174449","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-174450","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108379","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-108381","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174451","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-174452","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-174453","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174454","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-174455","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174456","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-174457","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108382","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174458","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-108384","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174459","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-174460","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-174461","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-108386","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174462","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-174463","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-174464","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-108388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174465","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-174466","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-174467","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-174468","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-108390","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108392","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108394","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174469","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-174470","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-174471","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-174472","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108393","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-108395","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174473","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-108396","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108399","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174474","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-108398","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174475","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-108400","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108402","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174476","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-174477","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-174478","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-174479","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108403","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-108405","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174480","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-174481","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-108406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174482","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-174483","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-108408","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108410","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174484","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-174485","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]}],"id":"blk-108411","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-108413","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174486","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-108414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174487","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-108415","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174488","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-174489","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-174490","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-174491","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108416","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-108418","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174492","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-174493","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-174494","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-174495","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-108419","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174496","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-174497","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-174498","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-108421","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174499","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-174500","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-174501","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-174502","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-108423","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174503","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-174504","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-174505","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-174506","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-108425","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108428","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174507","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-174508","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-108427","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174509","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-174510","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-108429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174511","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-174512","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-108431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174513","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-174514","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-108433","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174515","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-174516","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-108435","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174517","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-174518","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-108437","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174519","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-174520","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-174521","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-108439","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174522","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-174523","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-174524","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-108441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174525","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-174526","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-174527","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-108443","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108445","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174528","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]}],"id":"blk-108446","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-108448","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174529","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-174530","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-108449","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174531","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-174532","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-108451","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174533","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-174534","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-108453","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108456","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174535","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-108455","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-108457","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174536","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-174537","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agentelic or the user's own API key) processes. SpecPrompt is a tool, not an agent. The MCP server version ("},{"id":"spn-174538","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-174539","text":") returns the prompt for the agent to execute."}]}],"id":"blk-108458","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-108460","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-174540","text":"Phase 3: MCP Server (week 3)"}]},{"id":"blk-108461","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174541","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement MCP server"},{"id":"spn-174542","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-174543","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/mcp/server.ex"},{"id":"spn-174544","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-108462","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-108464","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174545","text":"JSON-RPC over HTTP, MCP protocol v2025-03-26"}]}],"id":"blk-108465","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108468","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-174546","text":"Tools: "},{"id":"spn-174547","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_validate"},{"id":"spn-174548","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174549","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_lint"},{"id":"spn-174550","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174551","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_generate"},{"id":"spn-174552","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174553","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_gen"},{"id":"spn-174554","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174555","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-174556","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174557","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_approve"},{"id":"spn-174558","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174559","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_diff"},{"id":"spn-174560","text":", "},{"id":"spn-174561","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_search"}]}],"id":"blk-108467","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-108470","ki